:: Island Landing
<<water>>
You swim past many large bunches of coral and jagged chunks of rock before reaching a warm and sandy beach where you pull yourself out of the water.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Island]]>><<set $islanddistance to 0>><<location "beach">><</link>>

:: Island Landing Boat
The ship pulls into a small inlet river and into a small oasis village. "Well, we're here. Get your stuff and get off."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Desert Village]]>><<set $islanddistance to 20>><<location "desert">><</link>>

:: Island
<<effects>>
<<if $stress gte $stressmax and !$possessed>>
	<<passoutisland>>
<<else>>
    <<if $islanddistance is 0>>
        <<location "beach">>
        <<set $chill_day to 0>>
        <<set _weather_display to "normal">>
        You're standing on the shore of the beach. Harsh waves lap at the sand.
    <<elseif $islanddistance lt 5>>
        <<location "beach">>
        <<set $chill_day to 0>>
        <<set _weather_display to "normal">>
        You're standing in the middle of a warm beach covered in fine soft sand. Even standing on it causes your feet to sink a bit deeper.
    <<elseif $islanddistance is 10>>
        <<location "desert">>
        <<set $chill_day to -120>>
        <<set _weather_display to "normal">>
        <<set $weather to "clear">>
        You find a massive mound of sand. It looks like some kind of insect nest.
    <<elseif $islanddistance is 20>>
        <<location "desert">>
        <<set $chill_day to -120>>
        <<set _weather_display to "normal">>
        <<set $weather to "clear">>
        You come across a small village resting on an oasis of water and palms.
    <<elseif $islanddistance lt 30>>
        <<location "desert">>
        <<set $chill_day to -120>>
        <<set _weather_display to "normal">>
        <<set $weather to "clear">>
        Sandy dunes stretch on ahead as the desert heat eats away at you.
    <<elseif $islanddistance is 30>>
        <<location "forest">>
        <<set $chill_day to 0>>
        <<set _weather_display to "normal">>
        <<set $weather to "rain">>
        The land slopes as the desert meets a mountain range full of lush vegetation.
    <<elseif $islanddistance is 40>>
        <<location "forest">>
        <<set $chill_day to 0>>
        <<set _weather_display to "normal">>
        <<set $weather to "rain">>
        As you climb the mountain path you find an old steel slag. Continuing down the path you find more and more until you come across a large plane. It lies rusting under a layer of overgrowth.
    <<elseif $islanddistance lt 50>>
        <<location "forest">>
        <<set $chill_day to 0>>
        <<set _weather_display to "normal">>
        <<set $weather to "rain">>
        The mountains continue to rise rife with vegetation. The treeline blots the sun although the moisture and humidity leave you miserable.
    <<elseif $islanddistance is 50>>
        <<location "snowforest">>
        <<set $chill_day to 150>>
        <<set $weather to "snow">>
        Halfway up the mountains, the cool air sets in as snow begins to fall lightly over the higher elevation pine trees.
    <<elseif $islanddistance is 55>>
        <<location "snowforest">>
        <<set $chill_day to 150>>
        <<set $weather to "snow">>
        While wandering the snowy landscape you find an old stone hut, a shattered see-through material lines the inside.
    <<elseif $islanddistance lt 60>>
        <<location "snowforest">>
        <<set $chill_day to 150>>
        <<set $weather to "snow">>
        The mountains are slick with soft snow. Animal prints dot the land as the pines tower over you.
    <<elseif $islanddistance is 60>>
        <<location "glacier">>
        <<set $chill_day to 150>>
        <<set $weather to "snow">>
        You reach the peak of the mountains and on the other side is an expansive glacial sheet that seems to stretch into the horizon
    <<elseif $islanddistance is 61>>
        <<location "glacier">>
        <<set $chill_day to 150>>
        <<set $weather to "snow">>
        Your feet hit the hard icy surface of the glacier and you’re met with freezing gusts of wind. Not much could survive up here. The clouds stuck from going over the mountain peaks leave a thick and permanent fog hanging over the land.
    <<elseif $islanddistance is 65>>
        <<location "glacier">>
        <<set $chill_day to 150>>
        <<set $weather to "snow">>
        As you walk further into the ice sheet you find an odd carved hole into the ice.
    <<elseif $islanddistance lte 70>>
        <<location "glacier">>
        <<set $chill_day to 150>>
        <<set $weather to "snow">>
        You're walking along a solid sheet of ice, various crags litter the landscape but not much else.
    <</if>>
    <br><br>
	<<set $danger to random(1, 10000)>><<set $dangerevent to 0>>
